10
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:26,000
Films generate income from several revenue streams, including theatrical
exhibition, home video, television broadcast rights, and merchandising.

11
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:34,000
However, theatrical box-office earnings are the primary metric for trade publications in assessing the success of a film, mostly because of the
availability of the data compared to sales figures for home video and broadcast rights, but also because of historical practice.

12
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:42,000
Included on the list are charts of the top box-office earners (ranked by both the nominal and real value of their revenue), a chart of high-grossing films by
calendar year, a timeline showing the transition of the highest-grossing film record, and a chart of the highest-grossing film franchises and series.

13
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:50,000
All charts are ranked by international theatrical box-office performance where possible,
excluding income derived from home video, broadcasting rights, and merchandise.

14
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Traditionally, war films, musicals, and historical dramas have been the most popular genres,
but franchise films have been among the best performers of the 21st century.

15
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:06,000
There is strong interest in the superhero genre, with eleven films in the
Marvel Cinematic Universe featuring among the nominal top-earners.

16
00:50:08,000 --> 00:50:14,000
The most successful superhero film, Avengers: Endgame, is also the second-highest-grossing film on the nominal earnings
chart, and there are four films in total based on the Avengers comic books charting in the top twenty.

17
00:53:16,000 --> 00:53:22,000
Other Marvel Comics adaptations have also had success with the Spider-Man and X-Men properties,
while films based on Batman and Superman from DC Comics have generally performed well.

18
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
Beyond the superhero genre, Star Wars is the most represented
franchise in the nominal earnings chart with five films.

19
00:59:32,000 --> 00:59:38,000
Although the nominal earnings chart is dominated by films adapted from pre-existing
properties and sequels, it is headed by Avatar, which is an original work.

20
01:02:40,000 --> 01:02:46,000
Animated family films have performed consistently well, with Disney films
enjoying lucrative re-releases prior to the home-video era.

21
01:05:48,000 --> 01:05:54,000
Disney also enjoyed later success with films such as Frozen and its sequel, Zootopia and its sequel, and The Lion King (along with its
computer-animated remake), as well as its Pixar division, of which Inside Out 2, Incredibles 2, and Toy Story 3 and 4 have been the best performers.

22
01:08:56,000 --> 01:09:02,000
Beyond Disney and Pixar animation, China's Ne Zha 2 (the highest-grossing animated film),
and the Despicable Me and Shrek series have met with the most success.

23
01:12:04,000 --> 01:12:10,000
While inflation has eroded the achievements of most films from the 1960s and 1970s,
there are franchises originating from that period that are still active.

24
01:15:12,000 --> 01:15:18,000
Besides the Star Wars franchise, James Bond films are still being released
periodically; both are among the highest-grossing franchises.

25
01:18:20,000 --> 01:18:26,000
Some of the older films that held the record of highest-grossing film still have respectable grosses by today's standards, but
no longer compete numerically against today's top-earners in an era of much higher individual ticket prices.

26
01:21:28,000 --> 01:21:34,000
When those prices are adjusted for inflation, however, then Gone with the Wind—which was the
highest-grossing film outright for twenty-five years—is still the highest-grossing film of all time.

27
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:42,000
All grosses on the list are expressed in U.S.

28
01:27:44,000 --> 01:27:50,000
dollars at their nominal value, except where stated otherwise.

